# Draft only. Do not promote this file into knowledge/graph or add it to the index.
id:                     DRAFT-highway-native-standalone-runner
trigger_tool:           cmake|ctest|conan|googletest
phase:                  configuration|testing
error_signature:        BUILD_TESTING.*googletest|GoogleTest.*download|gtest_discover_tests
severity:               2
category:               build-system|cmake|conan|testing|network
match_keywords:         BUILD_TESTING, HWY_TEST_STANDALONE, GoogleTest, gtest_discover_tests, CTest, offline
title:                  Prefer an upstream native standalone runner before disabling or vendoring a test framework
root_cause:             Some upstream projects provide a GTest-compatible native runner but leave it disabled by default, so a normal test configuration tries to bootstrap or link GoogleTest unnecessarily.
affected_scope:         CMake packages whose upstream runner implements the test-discovery command-line contract used by gtest_discover_tests.
verification_cmd:       cmake -DBUILD_TESTING=ON -DHWY_ENABLE_TESTS=ON -DHWY_ENABLE_CONTRIB=ON -DHWY_TEST_STANDALONE=ON <source>; ctest --output-on-failure --no-tests=error
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           enable-native-standalone-test-runner
rec_description:        Enable the maintained upstream standalone runner together with its test and CTest switches. Run it only on a runnable target and report its result independently from the consumer test.
rec_command:            CMakeToolchain(self).variables['HWY_TEST_STANDALONE'] = 'ON'; CMake(self).test(cli_args=['--output-on-failure', '--no-tests=error'])
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               opt-in-conan-test-option
forbid_1_pattern:       HWY_TEST_STANDALONE=ON.*(passed|100%)
forbid_1_reason:        Enabling a runner is configuration evidence, not execution evidence.
forbid_1_consequence:   The PR can falsely claim target-side coverage.
forbid_2_pattern:       BUILD_TESTING=OFF.*(complete|full).*test
forbid_2_reason:        Disabling an upstream suite cannot demonstrate its execution.
forbid_2_consequence:   The package loses upstream validation while overstating coverage.
similar_to:             [E017, E217, E221, E224]
doc_file:               knowledge/drafts/DRAFT-highway-native-standalone-runner.md
last_updated:           2026-08-14
source_event:           Highway 1.3.0 source inspection for OpenHarmony PC PR #3398
source_pr:              3398
metrics_success_count:  0
metrics_fail_count:     0
metrics_confidence:     0.0
draft:                  true
contributor_id:         ASP1
